[3c] why: three independent obstructions, each fatal on its own
   (i)  L=8 fixed => physical volume V = (8 aL)^4 shrinks with a:
        beta 2.2 -> 2.75:  aL ratio = 4.000e+00,  V ratio = 2.561e+02
        beta 2.5 -> 4.0:  aL ratio = 4.650e+01,  V ratio = 4.676e+06
        beta 2.5 -> 6.0:  aL ratio = 8.535e+03,  V ratio = 5.308e+15
   (ii) a(beta) has no absolute value in-window: two-loop at beta=2.5 gives m*a = 0.023 vs the
        measured 1.707 (B04.md:64, factor 74), and a(2.5)/a(6) = 8535 (GW7-FIXEDA-SCAN.md:92).
        Without a(beta) there is no a^2 axis -- only a beta axis.
   (iii) m_fit is a UV reading, not a physical mass: mhat = 1.69..4.00 at every beta
        (xi/a = 1/1.707 = 0.586 at beta=2.5, B04.md:98) => Delta_a = mhat/aL ~ 1/aL grows
        by 4 decades as beta grows: that IS the 'no continuum limit' statement, not a mass.

